# Empty on purpose — do not fill this in.
#
# Production serves the SPA from nginx, which proxies /api to the gateway on
# localhost:8080, so every request must go out as a relative URL. An empty
# VITE_API_URL is what produces that.
#
# This file exists because `vite build` runs in production mode and therefore
# never reads .env.development. Without it VITE_API_URL resolves to undefined,
# and shared/infrastructure/http/client.ts plus asset-url.ts request
# `undefined/api/...` — every API call and all 3D model loading fails, in a
# bundle that builds and deploys without a single warning. That is why the
# value is pinned here rather than left to whoever runs the build to remember.
#
# Tracked deliberately: .gitignore excludes .env.*, so this file is committed
# with `git add -f`, the same way .env.development and .env.example are. It
# holds no secret — an empty value is the whole point.
VITE_API_URL=
